{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1f0-f342-7821-939e-4786eeeb7588"},"sequence":317,"recorded_at":1780531400000629,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1f1-b684-79b1-bff9-40061f826fc0"},"task_id":"01a0b1f1-b684-79b1-bff9-40061f826fc0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1f1-b684-79b1-bff9-40061f826fc0","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(979 line(s) above)\n980|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n981|not aggregate equality.\n982|\n983|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n984|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n985|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n986|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n987|\n988|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n989|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n990|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n991|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n992|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n993|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n994|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n995|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n996|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n997|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n998|   the capability registry row.\n999|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n1000|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n1001|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n1002|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n1003|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n1004|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n1005|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n1006|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n1007|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n1008|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n1009|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n1010|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n1011|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n1012|   literal <code>true</code>.\n1013|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n1014|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n1015|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n1016|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n1017|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n1018|\n1019|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n1020|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n1021|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n1022|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n1023|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n1024|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n1025|\n1026|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n1027|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n1028|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n1029|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n1030|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n1031|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n1032|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n1033|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n1034|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n1035|validate the boundary.\n1036|\n1037|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1038|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1039|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1040|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1041|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
