{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5cf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1f0-f342-7821-939e-4786eeeb7588"},"sequence":322,"recorded_at":1780531400000639,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1f1abd4708d921179d07d7eb84e","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`.\n(979 line(s) above)\n980|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n981|not aggregate equality.\n982|\n983|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n984|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n985|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n986|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n987|\n988|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n989|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n990|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n991|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n992|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n993|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n994|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n995|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n996|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n997|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n998|   the capability registry row.\n999|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n1000|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n1001|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n1002|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n1003|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n1004|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n1005|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n1006|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n1007|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n1008|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n1009|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n1010|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n1011|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n1012|   literal <code>true</code>.\n1013|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n1014|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n1015|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n1016|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n1017|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n1018|\n1019|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n1020|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n1021|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n1022|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n1023|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n1024|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n1025|\n1026|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n1027|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n1028|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n1029|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n1030|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n1031|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n1032|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n1033|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n1034|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n1035|validate the boundary.\n1036|\n1037|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1038|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1039|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1040|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1041|\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1f0-f342-7821-939e-4786eeeb7588"},"sequence":323,"recorded_at":1780531400000641,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1f1af51742681c8b8543353b4c7","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-13-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"^### 13\\\\.1\\\\|^## 13\\\\|^### 5\\\\.2\\\\|^## 5\\\\b\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md | head; echo ===; sed -n '1956,2010p' internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Find 13.1, 5.2 and read terminal events\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"1489:## 5. Domain records and state machine\\n1808:### 5.2 Session Event\\n9172:## 13. End-to-end lifecycle flows\\n9178:### 13.1 Direct-session launch\\n10102:### 13.10 Resume\\n10199:### 13.11 Reboot restore\\n10224:### 13.12 Failure and recovery matrix\\n10248:### 13.13 Crash/restart outcome gate\\n10322:### 13.14 Cross-environment clone\\n11266:### 13.15 Directory continuation planning and execution\\n===\\n#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\\n\\nSession Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\\nlease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\\nchanges exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\\n<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\\nthe definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\\n\\n| Event type | Exact payload members |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\\n| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\\n\\nThe binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\\nInstance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\\nreplicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\\nManifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\\nbackend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\\nreference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\\nterminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\\n\\n<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\\nauthorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\\nthat owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\\nadmitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\\ndoes not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\\nAttach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\\nOwner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\\nas inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\\nversion replacement.\\n\\n### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\\n\\nThe Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\\n<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\\n\\n| Field | Type | Constraint |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\\n| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\\n| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical Lease Record digest |\\n| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\\n| <code>lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 | Cryptographically random unique fencing token |\\n| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Lease scope |\\n| <code>epoch</code> | uint53 | Starts at 1; never decreases |\\n| <code>holder_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Proposed owner |\\n| <code>predecessor_lease_id</code> | UUIDv4 or null | Null only at epoch 1 |\\n| <code>reason</code> | enum | <code>create</code>, <code>graceful_takeover</code>, <code>force_takeover</code>, <code>recovery</code> |\\n| <code>checkpoint_id</code> | digest or null | Null only for epoch-1 <code>create</code>; otherwise the validated materialized handoff base |\\n| <code>issued_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Initiator |\\n| <code>created_by_host_id</code> | UUIDv7 | MUST equal <code>issued_by_host_id</code> |\\n| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\\n| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\\n\\nThe object is closed; every row is required, including nullable fields.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4117,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1030,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
