{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9ad","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1f0-f342-7821-939e-4786eeeb7588"},"sequence":817,"recorded_at":1780531400001629,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c7ad7d78-80b9-46e1-9367-f83a27084d43"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1f3d1c676248cc0cdc01839ddd6","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-38-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"type LeaseSummary\\\" -A 20 internal/sessrepo/*.go | grep -v _test | head -30; echo ===; sed -n '1,60p' internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py\",\n  \"description\": \"Read LeaseSummary and harness head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go:142:type LeaseSummary struct {\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-143-\\tRecordID       string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-144-\\tSessionID      string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-145-\\tLeaseID        string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-146-\\tEpoch          uint64\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-147-\\tHolderHostID   string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-148-\\tPredecessor    string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-149-\\tHasPredecessor bool\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-150-\\tCheckpoint     string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-151-\\tHasCheckpoint  bool\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-152-\\tReason         string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-153-}\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-154-\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-155-// FencingToken is a presented ownership proof: the epoch, lease ID, and\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-156-// holder the presenter claims.\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-157-type FencingToken struct {\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-158-\\tEpoch        uint64\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-159-\\tLeaseID      string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-160-\\tHolderHostID string\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-161-}\\ninternal/sessrepo/lease_store.go-162-\\n===\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Narrowing-mutant harness for internal/axpane.\\n\\nEvery gate ships a narrowing mutant: the gate stays present and is\\nweakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\\nthe named killer test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that\\nthe gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\n\\nEach row runs M (mutate one production file in place), R (run the\\nscoped Go killer through the production entry point), V (verdict from\\nthe Go exit code plus a FAIL kill-line: KILLED iff R fails with a test\\nfailure line, SURVIVED iff R passes, ERROR for anything else —\\nunapplied patches, build breaks, timeouts). M failures and R\\ninfrastructure errors are ERROR, never kills or survivals. The file is\\nrestored from its backup after every row, pass or fail.\\n\\nRow C-doc-comment is the harmless control: a comment-only edit that\\nmust SURVIVE, proving the harness observes test outcomes instead of\\nhard-coding kills.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py\\n  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py N-config\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport os\\nimport shutil\\nimport subprocess\\nimport sys\\nimport tempfile\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\\nPACKAGE = \\\"internal/axpane\\\"\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Mutant:\\n    name: str\\n    path: str\\n    find: str\\n    replace: str\\n    count: int\\n    run: str\\n    expect: str\\n    note: str\\n\\n\\nMUTANTS = [\\n    Mutant(\\n        name=\\\"N-config\\\",\\n        path=f\\\"{PACKAGE}/decide.go\\\",\\n        find=\\\"\\\\tif input.ConfigErr != nil {\\\\n\\\",\\n        replace=\\\"\\\\tif input.ConfigErr != nil && input.Mode == ModeRestore {\\\\n\\\",\\n        count=1,\\n        run=\\\"TestDecideTable/refused_config_invalid\\\",\\n        expect=\\\"KILLED\\\",\\n        note=\\\"Admits exactly launch-mode invalid config; restore-mode still refuses.\\\",\\n    ),\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3107,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 777,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
